# motoquencer `pattern` inside a song `form` (issue #54). The manual's rule for
# everything that shapes the movement is that it applies "within each individual
# part", and the `form` row confirms the parts themselves just move forwards.
#
# form 5 (AB) over eight steps gives A = 0..3 and B = 4..7. Pattern 1 walks its
# two-forward-one-back figure inside A -- 0,1,2, 1,2,3, 2,3 -- and only then, when
# the figure would step past the end of A, moves on to B and walks the identical
# figure there: 4,5,6, 5,6,7, 6,7. `startofpart` (O3) fires on each part entry;
# `startofsequence` (O2) only at the top of the complete form.
#
# So a pattern does NOT run across the part boundary, and the cycle that advances
# the form is the same "forward progress crossed the end" event as without a form.
# Step numbers do not fit on an output jack (they clamp at +/-10 V), so
# `currentstep` rides an internal cable scaled by 1/10: step N reads N/10.
tickrate 100
patch <<<
[m4]
[m4]
[motoquencer]
    clock           = I1
    numsteps        = 8
    numfaders       = 8
    pattern         = 1
    form            = 5
    currentstep     = _CS
    startofpart     = O3
    startofsequence = O2
[copy]
    input  = _CS * 0.1
    output = O1
>>>
@2 set I1 1
@2 expect O1 0 tol 1e-4
@2 expect O2 1 tol 1e-4
@2 expect O3 1 tol 1e-4
@3 set I1 0
@4 set I1 1
@4 expect O1 0.1 tol 1e-4
@4 expect O2 0 tol 1e-4
@4 expect O3 0 tol 1e-4
